program while_loop

? `while COND do` is the plain while-true loop: same AST and codegen as
? bare `loop till`, but it reads as written (`till` keeps its historical
? semantics for back-compat).

@ main ||:
	n: 0
	while n < 3 do
		print|n|
		n = n + 1
	$
	m: 10
	while m > 8 do
		print|m|
		m = m - 1
	$
	print|["0", "1", "2", "10", "9"]|
$
